2. SOLDIER TROOP SYSTEM
================================================================================

Troop Categories (4) and Counter Cycle (VERIFIED):
- SPEARMAN counters CAVALRY  | countered by BOWMAN
- BOWMAN counters SPEARMAN   | countered by SHIELDMAN
- SHIELDMAN counters BOWMAN  | countered by CAVALRY
- CAVALRY counters SHIELDMAN | countered by SPEARMAN

Counter mechanics (VERIFIED):
- Counter (attacker advantage): ATK +40% vs that troop type, and ignores 20%
  of the target's DMG Reduction
- Countered (attacker disadvantage): ATK -40% vs the countering type

Troop Levels: 1 to 6 (6 = maximum)
- Upgraded at Drill Ground: crop + exp scroll (timed), or scroll (instant, no cost)

Troop Sub-Types (24 total = 6 per category, VERIFIED from hero possession data):
- SPEARMAN:  Longspearman | Lancer | Dagger-axe Soldier | Modao Soldier |
             Long Swordsman | Twin Spearman
- SHIELDMAN: Saber & Shield | Heavy Shield | Spear & Shield | Hammer & Shield |
             Sword & Shield | Axe & Shield
- BOWMAN:    Longbowman | Crossbowman | Toxibowman | Hunter |
             Improved Crossbowman | Fire Bowman
- CAVALRY:   Sword Cavalry | Spear Cavalry | Broadsword Cavalry | Heavy Cavalry |
             Bow Cavalry | Axe Cavalry

Troop Selection (VERIFIED):
- Session start: pick 1 of 3 offered troops (e.g. Longspearman, Saber & Shield,
  Heavy Shield); options can be rerolled unlimited times before confirming
- New troop picks unlock at Barracks level 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 / 12 (5 picks)
- Summoning a hero auto-grants their possessed troop type; if already owned,
  the player gets a free new troop pick at the Barracks

Per-Soldier Stat Format (VERIFIED from Soldier screenshots):
- HP, ATK
- Rage initial/full (e.g. 4/6 = starts battle with 4 Rage; skill ready at 6)
- Move range (tiles, shoe icon) and ATK range (tiles, sword icon)
- Crop consumption per soldier
- 4 soldiers per tile

NOTE: The previous T1-T6 / INFANTRY / RANGED / SIEGE data here was fabricated
and has been removed. Per-sub-type numeric stats (HP/ATK/Rage/ranges/crop for
levels 1-6) must be re-captured from the Soldier and Soldier lv 6 folders.

