4. HERO SYSTEM
================================================================================

HERO SYSTEM (VERIFIED - source: "Hero Skill and Expertise.md", authoritative)
================================================================================

TOTAL: 59 heroes in game. 56 documented below (3 unidentified - pending).

HERO DATA FORMAT (per hero):
- Name (courtesy name) | Skill title | Possession: troop sub-type
- HP+ [x-y] and ATK+ [x-y]: random ranges rolled on acquisition/redraw
- Skill: passive battle effect
- Unique Hero Rare Expertise: exclusive to this hero only

{Soldier} PARAMETER CONVENTION (VERIFIED from user):
- "{Soldier}" = the hero's possessed troop sub-type ONLY
- Named category (e.g. "Spearman", "Shieldman") = buff applies to ALL soldiers
  of that category
- "All allies" = every allied soldier regardless of type

EXPERTISE SYSTEM (VERIFIED):
- Slots: 1 Common + 1 Uncommon + 1 Rare (available from hero level 1)
- Chosen level (max tier, reached after 100 redraws): +1 extra expertise slot
- Stacking: Common up to 3x, Uncommon up to 2x, Rare not stackable
- A hero's expertise pool = category Common/Uncommon/Rare lists
  + sub-type Unique Rare list + the hero's own Unique Hero Rare
- Redraw: reroll expertise using Hero Fragments (from General Muster Terrace)

HERO PROGRESSION & DEATH (VERIFIED):
- 7 level tiers: Level 1 (base) to Chosen (max)
- 100 redraws -> Chosen level
- Summon heroes at Hall of Heroes level 1/5/10/15 (4 heroes per session)
- Summoning a hero auto-grants their possessed troop; if already owned,
  free Barracks re-pick
- Death vs enemy: hero imprisoned in enemy Iron Prison (duration scales with
  Iron Prison building level; unlocks at Hall of Heroes level 5)
- Death on unowned monster plot: 4-hour cooldown, then re-summonable

